course: dictionary
lesson: 13724
title: Intact: whole and unharmed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Intact is a word you will meet in stories, news and science. It means whole, with nothing broken or missing. «The egg landed on the grass and was still intact.» The egg did not crack, so it is intact.
explain: Intact can also mean still the same as before, not harmed or changed. «After the storm, the old bridge was still intact.» The bridge did not fall down, so the storm did not harm it. Look at the words around intact to decide which meaning fits.
explain: You will often see intact with other words: remain intact, stay intact, keep something intact. If a vase stays intact, it stays whole. If you keep your confidence intact, a setback does not take it away.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in "whole and unharmed". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Intact means whole, not damaged or broken, with nothing missing.
fact: Intact can also mean still the same as before, not harmed or changed.
fact: Common phrases are remain intact, stay intact, fully intact and keep something intact.
fact: Scientists in an egg drop test check whether the egg stays intact after a fall.
fact: Intact does not change its form, so we say fully intact, not more intact.
exercise: «The egg landed on the grass and was still intact.» What does intact mean here? | Very cold | Thrown far away | *Whole and not cracked | Covered in mud
exercise: «After the storm, the old bridge was still intact.» Find and copy the one word that tells us the bridge was not harmed. | old | bridge | storm | *intact
exercise: Mia says, «The vase fell, but it stayed intact.» What does stayed intact suggest? | It fell into the sea | It was made of paper | *It did not break | It was broken into pieces
test: «She kept her confidence intact after the bad test.» What does this suggest? | She asked for help | She had no confidence at all | *Her confidence was not harmed or changed | She lost all her confidence
test: «The science team checked that all the eggs were intact after the drop.» What does intact mean? | Cracked and sticky | Thrown far away | *Whole, with nothing broken | Missing a shell
exam: Ben says, «I want the cake to stay intact until the party.» What does intact mean in this sentence? | Eaten by the dog | Cut into small slices | Sold at the shop | *Still whole and not damaged
